`HL7Ingestor` parses inbound HL7v2 messages for our EHR pipeline. It's a 300-line class that validates, parses, and routes. The painful part is a class-level schema cache that is warmed once and shared across every ingestor instance in the worker — profiles registered at runtime by one ingestor must be visible to all of them (we register site-specific segment overrides during startup and then spin up per-thread ingestors). No test suite; behaviour must be bit-identical. Keep the import path `pipeline.hl7.HL7Ingestor` and the `.ingest(raw)` API. Python 3.11+, no new deps.

