This `@timed` decorator is applied to ~150 service methods and a handful of module-level helper functions. A Grafana exporter reads `METRICS` and wants per-class rollups, so we need timings grouped by the owning class name in addition to the flat qualname buckets we have now. Introspection must stay intact — `inspect.signature` is read by our RPC schema generator.

```python
import time
import functools

METRICS = {}

def timed(fn):
    @functools.wraps(fn)
    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):
        t0 = time.perf_counter()
        try:
            return fn(*args, **kwargs)
        finally:
            dt = time.perf_counter() - t0
            METRICS.setdefault(fn.__qualname__, []).append(dt)
    return wrapper


class Billing:
    @timed
    def charge(self, account, cents):
        ...

@timed
def reconcile(ledger):     # module-level helper, also decorated
    ...
```

