    @cached_property
    def schema(self):
        return {"endpoints": [f"{self._base_url}/users"]}
```

What I preserved: `session` and `schema` each compute at most once per instance (cached_property writes into `self.__dict__`, so later reads hit the instance dict and never re-run the builder). Unknown attribute access raises the standard `AttributeError` again now that `__getattr__` is gone. The public read API (`client.session`, `client.schema`) is unchanged.

